<title>SRI LANKA: Lanka Lubricants up 8 pct on results.</title>
<headline>Lanka Lubricants up 8 pct on results.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Lanka Lubricants Ltd rose eight percent or four rupees to 54 in early Thursday trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The price is rising on recently published first quarter results, which have been very good,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>The company said profits in the first three months to March 31, 1997, rose 55 percent to 60.59 million rupees.</p>
<p>Lanka Lubricants is the sole local manufacturer and distributor or lubricants in Sri Lanka. The company is a subsidiary of Caltex Petroleum Corp, which is a joint venture between U.S oil giants Texaco Inc and Chevron Corp.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
